{"name":"Bridle Path","hex":"#a29682","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bridle path","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An established trail used by riders mounted on horses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bridle_path"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bridal Path (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Bridal Path is a novel by Scottish author Nigel Tranter, first published in 1952. In 1959 a film version The Bridal Path was released."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/02/TheBridalPath.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bridal_Path_(novel)"},{"title":"The Bridal Path (film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Bridal Path is a 1959 British comedy film directed by Frank Launder and starring Bill Travers, George Cole and Bernadette O'Farrell. It is based on the 1952 novel of the same name by Nigel Tranter. The film was an unsuccessful attempt to repeat the success of Launder and Gilliat's earlier Geordie (1955)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/94/%22The_Bridal_Path%22_%281959_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Bridal_Path_(film)"},{"title":"Bridle path","blocks":[{"text":"A bridle path, also bridleway, equestrian trail, horse riding path, ride, bridle road, or horse trail, is a trail or a thoroughfare that is used by people riding on horses. Trails originally created for use by horses often now serve a wider range of users, including equestrians, hikers, and cyclists. Such paths are either impassable for motorized vehicles, or vehicles are banned. The laws relating to allowable uses vary from country to country."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Hillingdon_bridleway.JPG/330px-Hillingdon_bridleway.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bridle_path"},{"title":"Bridle","blocks":[{"text":"A bridle is a piece of equipment used to direct a horse. It includes both the headstall that holds a bit that goes in the mouth of a horse, and the reins that are attached to the bit. It provides additional control and communication through rein pressure. The trade that makes bridles is a saddler."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Hunt_bridle_head.jpg/330px-Hunt_bridle_head.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bridle"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Oritkarinranta_Oulu_20140701.jpg/500px-Oritkarinranta_Oulu_20140701.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Oritkarinranta_Oulu_20140701.jpg/1280px-Oritkarinranta_Oulu_20140701.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Oritkarinranta_Oulu_20140701.jpg/500px-Oritkarinranta_Oulu_20140701.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A horse riding path in Oulu, Finland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOritkarinranta_Oulu_20140701.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f9/National_Horse_Trail_Marker.jpg/500px-National_Horse_Trail_Marker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f9/National_Horse_Trail_Marker.jpg/500px-National_Horse_Trail_Marker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Marker for the National Horse Trail in Australia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANational_Horse_Trail_Marker.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Bridleway_in_Ettington%2C_Warwicksh